            "fame": 54,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le corridor du Wakhan ou corridor de Wakhan est un étroit corridor géographique situé dans la province du Badakhchan, dans l'Est de l'Afghanistan. Il est aussi surnommé « bec de canard ».",
                "en": "The Wakhan Corridor is a protruding strip of territory mostly in the Wakhan District of Badakhshan Province in northeastern Afghanistan. Smaller parts of it are within the Gorno-Badakhshan in eastern Tajikistan. It begins east of Ishkashim District and stretches eastward to the Wakhjir Pass, which connects by road Afghanistan with the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region of China. The strip narrowly separates Gorno-Badakhshan in Tajikistan from Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Gilgit-Baltistan in Pakistan."
            }
