            "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/",
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Syri_i_Kalter.jpg",
            "fame": 21,
            "description": {
                "fr": "L'Œil bleu est une source et un phénomène naturel situé dans le village de Muzinë, dans le sud de l'Albanie. Attraction touristique populaire, l'eau bleu clair de la rivière peut être vue à une profondeur de plus de cinquante mètres.",
                "en": "The Blue Eye is a water spring and natural phenomenon occurring in the village of Muzinë in Finiq municipality, southern Albania. A popular tourist attraction, the clear blue water of the river can be seen from a depth of more than fifty metres. Divers have descended to fifty metres, but it is still unclear what the actual depth of the karst hole is. This phenomenon is also known as \"springs of Bistricë\" as it is the initial water source of Bistricë river, 25 km long, which ends in the Ionian Sea south of Sarandë."
            }
