            "fame": 101,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La forêt amazonienne est une forêt équatoriale d'Amérique du Sud couvrant la totalité du bassin amazonien ainsi que des zones périphériques comme le plateau des Guyanes. Elle s'étend sur neuf pays, principalement au Brésil.",
                "en": "The Amazon rainforest, also called the Amazon jungle, Amazonia, or simply the Amazon, is a moist broadleaf tropical rainforest in the Amazon biome that covers most of the Amazon basin of South America. This basin encompasses 7 million km2, of which 6 million km2 are covered by the rainforest. This region includes territory belonging to nine nations and 3,344 indigenous territories."
            }
