            "description": {
                "fr": "La réserve de faune du Dja est une réserve faunique située au sud-est du Cameroun et établie comme réserve de biosphère en 1981.",
                "en": "Dja Faunal Reserve, located in southeastern Cameroon, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site inscribed in 1987. Causes of inscription include diversity of species present in the park, the presence of five threatened species of mammal, and lack of disturbance within the park. It is managed by Dja Conservation Services, which is led by a conservator. The Reserve receives significant support for its management from many projects funded by international partners and supporters of conservation in Cameroon."
            }
