            "fame": 64,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le Grand Bouddha de Leshan est une statue monumentale de Bouddha taillée dans la falaise du mont Lingyun, sur la rive est de la rivière Min dans la région du mont Emei, au Sichuan.",
                "en": "The Leshan Giant Buddha is a 71-meter tall stone statue, built between 712 and 804 AD. It is carved out of a cliff face of Cretaceous red bed sandstones that lies at the confluence of the Min River and Dadu River in the southern part of Sichuan Province in China, near the city of Leshan. The stone sculpture faces Mount Emei, with the rivers flowing below its feet. It is the largest and tallest stone Buddha statue in the world and it is by far the tallest pre-modern statue in the world. It is over 4 kilometers from the Wuyou Temple."
            }
