            "description": {
                "fr": "La cathédrale de sel est une église construite à l'intérieur des mines de sel de Zipaquirá, dans la Savane de Bogota, dans le département de Cundinamarca, en Colombie. C'est aussi un lieu de culte et l'un des sanctuaires catholiques les plus connus parmi ceux consacrés au chemin de croix de Jésus-Christ.",
                "en": "The Salt Cathedral of Zipaquirá is an underground Roman Catholic church built within the tunnels of a salt mine 200 metres underground in a halite mountain near the city of Zipaquirá, in Cundinamarca, Colombia. It is a tourist destination and place of pilgrimage in the country. The temple at the bottom has three sections, representing the birth, life, and death of Jesus. The icons, ornaments and architectural details are hand carved in the halite rock. Some marble sculptures are included."
            }
