            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santa_Catalina_Arch_-_Antigua_Guatemala_Feb_2020.jpg",
            "fame": 70,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Antigua Guatemala, plus connue sous le nom d'Antigua, est l'ancienne capitale du royaume de Guatemala. La ville est connue pour son architecture coloniale de style baroque et de Renaissance espagnole et pour ses ruines causées par les deux tremblements de terre de 1773.",
                "en": "Antigua Guatemala, commonly known as Antigua or La Antigua, is a city in the central highlands of Guatemala. The city was the capital of the Captaincy General of Guatemala from 1543 through 1773, with much of its Baroque-influenced architecture and layout dating from that period. Antigua Guatemala serves as the capital of the homonymous municipality and the Sacatepéquez Department."
            }
