            "fame": 40,
            "description": {
                "fr": "L'archipel indonésien des Raja Ampat est situé près de la côte nord-ouest de la Nouvelle-Guinée, dans la province de Papouasie du Sud-Ouest.",
                "en": "Raja Ampat, or the Four Kings, is an archipelago located off the northwest tip of Bird's Head Peninsula, Southwest Papua province, Indonesia. It comprises over 1,500 small islands, cays, and shoals around the four main islands of Misool, Salawati, Batanta, and Waigeo, and the smaller island of Kofiau. The Raja Ampat archipelago is just south of the equator and forms part of the Coral Triangle, an area of Southeast Asian seas containing the richest marine biodiversity on earth."
            }
