            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_Gate_in_New_Delhi_03-2016.jpg",
            "fame": 51,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La porte de l'Inde, en anglais India Gate, est un monument aux morts situé à New Delhi en Inde, sur l'avenue dite Rajpath, au pied de la Colline de Raisina.",
                "en": "The India Gate is a war memorial arch that’s located near the Rajpath on the eastern edge of the \"ceremonial axis\" of New Delhi, India. It stands as a memorial to exactly 74,187 Indian soldiers of the British Indian Army who died between 1914 and 1921 during the First World War, in places like France, Flanders, Mesopotamia, Persia, East Africa, Gallipoli, in the Near and Far East, and the 1919 Third Anglo-Afghan War."
            }
