            "fame": 21,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Jabal al-Qal'a ou citadelle d'Amman en français est un site historique national situé au cœur d'Amman, capitale de la Jordanie. Sise au sommet d'une colline en forme de L, elle est l'une des sept jabal qui formaient la ville antique. Il est aujourd'hui un musée archéologique en plein-air.",
                "en": "The Amman Citadel on Citadel Hill is an archaeological site on an L-shaped hill towering over Downtown Amman, in the central part of the capital of Jordan. The Amman Citadel is considered to be among the world's oldest continuously inhabited places. Evidence of inhabitance since the Neolithic period has been found and the hill was fortified during the Bronze Age. The hill became the capital of the Kingdom of Ammon, sometime after 1200 BCE."
            }
