                "en": "Likiep Atoll is a coral atoll of 65 islands in the Pacific Ocean, and forms a legislative district of the Ratak Chain of the Marshall Islands. It is approximately 55 kilometers northwest of Wotje. Its total land area is only 10.26 square kilometers, but that encloses a deep central lagoon of 424 square kilometers. Likiep Atoll also possesses the Marshall Islands' highest point, an unnamed knoll 10 meters above sea level. The population of Likiep Atoll was 228 in 2021."
