            "fame": 50,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le parc national du Banc-d'Arguin est une réserve naturelle de Mauritanie. Couvrant un tiers du littoral mauritanien, il a une surface de 12 000 km2 partagés entre partie maritime et partie continentale. Le parc national du Banc-d'Arguin est donc un des plus grands parcs d'Afrique de l'Ouest.",
                "en": "The Banc d'Arguin National Park of Bay of Arguin lies in Western Africa on the west coast of Mauritania between Nouakchott and Nouadhibou and is the former mouth of the Tamanrasset River. The World Heritage Site is a major site for migratory birds and breeding birds, including flamingos, pelicans and terns. Much of the breeding is on sand banks including the islands of Tidra, Niroumi, Nair, Kijji and Arguim."
            }
