            "description": {
                "fr": "Le Barú ou Volcán de Chiriquí est un volcan endormi de la cordillère de Talamanca, à l'Ouest du Panama. Il constitue le point culminant du pays avec 3 474 mètres d'altitude. Sa riche végétation est protégée au nord par un parc national.",
                "en": "The Volcán Barú is an active stratovolcano and the tallest mountain in Panama, at 3,475 metres high. It lies about 35 km off the border of Costa Rica. It is also the twelfth highest peak in Central America. Due to its height and the narrowness of the isthmus of Panama, it is possible to see both the Pacific Ocean and Caribbean Sea from Volcán Barú's peak on a clear day."
            }
