            "description": {
                "fr": "L'archipel de San Blas ou îles San Blas, parfois appelé archipel des Mulatas, est un archipel côtier du Panama, situé dans la mer des Caraïbes. Il appartient administrativement à la comarque Guna Yala.",
                "en": "The San Blas Islands of Panama is an archipelago comprising approximately 365 islands and cays, of which 49 are inhabited. They lie off the north coast of the Isthmus of Panama, east of the Panama Canal. A part of the comarca Guna Yala along the Caribbean coast of Panama, it is home to the Kuna people. San Blas and its surrounding area is a haven for ecotourism because of its pristine environs. The area is also popular for sailing, as it is known for its beauty and lack of hurricanes."
            }
