            "fame": 47,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le Jardin botanique de Singapour est un jardin botanique d'une superficie de 74 hectares de la ville de Singapour. En 2015, ce jardin botanique est inscrit au patrimoine mondial de l'UNESCO et il reçoit quatre millions de visiteurs. Sa superficie est en 2021 de 82 hectares, ce qui représente plus de la moitié des Jardins botaniques royaux de Kew ou un quart de la superficie de Central Park à New York.",
                "en": "The Singapore Botanic Gardens is a tropical garden located at the fringe of the Orchard Road shopping district in Singapore. It is one of three gardens, and the only tropical garden, to be honoured as a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The Botanic Gardens was founded at its present site in 1859 by the Agri-horticultural Society. It played a pivotal role in the region's rubber trade boom in the early twentieth century when its first scientific director, Henry Nicholas Ridley, headed research into the plant's cultivation."
            }
