            "license": "Public domain",
            "licenseUrl": null,
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ommayyad_masjed.jpg",
            "fame": 78,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La grande mosquée des Omeyyades de Damas, construite entre 706 et 715, est un édifice religieux musulman bâti par le calife omeyyade Al Walid Ier.",
                "en": "The Umayyad Mosque, also known as the Great Mosque of Damascus, located in the old city of Damascus, the capital of Syria, is one of the largest and oldest mosques in the world. It is considered to be the oldest mosque still in use in its original form. It innovated and influenced nascent Islamic architecture by introducing a more organized and monumental design compared to earlier mosques."
            }
