            "fame": 123,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Funafuti est un atoll des Tuvalu, un état archipélagique d'Océanie. Il constitue la capitale de ce royaume et abrite sa plus grande ville, Vaiaku, où siègent le gouvernement et les institutions. L'aéroport international de Funafuti s'y trouve.",
                "en": "Funafuti is an atoll, comprising numerous islets, that is the capital of Tuvalu. As of the 2017 census, it has a population of 6,320 people. More people live in Funafuti than the rest of Tuvalu combined, with it containing approximately 60% of the nation's population. It is the world's easternmost capital of a sovereign state. The main islet, Fongafale, hosts Vaiaku, the administrative centre of the nation. Funafuti was first sighted by Europeans in 1819 by Arent Schuyler de Peyster, an American sea captain, who named it Ellice's Island. Between 1850 and 1875."
            }
