                "fr": "Bequia est la plus grande île des Grenadines dans les Caraïbes. Elle fait partie de Saint-Vincent-et-les-Grenadines",
                "en": "Bequia is the second-largest island in the Grenadines at 7 square miles. It is part of the country of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines and lies approximately 15 kilometres from the nation's capital, Kingstown, on the main island, Saint Vincent. The name Bequia is said to derive from the Carib word becouya, meaning \"island of the clouds\". The island's early inhabitants were the Kalinago, who lived throughout the Grenadines before the arrival of Europeans."
