            "fame": 25,
            "description": {
                "fr": "L’île de Pentecôte est l’une des 83 îles de l’archipel du Vanuatu, dans la province de Pénama. Elle se situe à 190 km au nord de la capitale, Port-Vila. En 2009, elle était peuplée de 16 843 habitants. Le premier Européen à avoir découvert l’île fut l’explorateur français Louis Antoine de Bougainville, le 22 mai 1768.",
                "en": "Pentecost is one of the 83 islands that make up the South Pacific nation of Vanuatu. It lies 190 kilometres due north of capital Port Vila. Pentecost is known as Pentecôte in French and Pentekos in Bislama. The island was known in its native languages by names such as Vanu Aroaroa, although these names are not in common use today. Pentecost has also been referred to as Raga or Araga, a tribal name that originated in the north but is now widely applied to the whole island. In old sources, it is occasionally referred to as Whitsuntide Island."
            }
